    "text_full": "Skip to content\nAbout Us\nPrograms\nNews & Media\nDONATE\nFR\nHERITAGE MINUTES\nPODCASTS\nVIDEOS\nEDUCATION GUIDES\nSEARCH PRODUCTIONS\nAbout Us\nCareers\nBoard of Directors\nStaff\nSupporters\nPolicies\nContact\nHome\n / About Us\nAbout Us\nHistorica Canada is a charitable organization that offers programs in both official languages that you can use to explore, learn, reflect on our history, and consider what it means to be Canadian.\n\nAll our programs are offered free of charge in both of our country’s official languages – and in addition, The Canadian Encyclopedia is available in 35 other languages. Our online programs and resources are accessed by more than 28 million users annually, and our educational tools have been distributed to more than 65,000 teachers from coast-to-coast-to-coast.\n\nHistory is best taught and learned through a wide variety of voices and insights into our past. In doing so, we better understand the scale and scope of achievements by individuals and by our country overall - as well as those areas where we failed.\n\nIn all our programs, we place a premium on accuracy and context, and work with subject matter experts toward those ends. While an event happens once, it can be seen from many different perspectives.  We look to ensure that our material addressing the stories, achievements and challenges of Canada reflect, as much as possible, the views of those directly affected\n\nAs a charitable organization, Historica Canada is supported by a variety of sources, including governments, corporate sponsors, and individuals. If you wish to support our work through a donation, you may do so here.\n\nHistorica Canada is a charitable organization that offers programs in both official languages that you can use to explore, learn, reflect on our history, and consider what it means to be Canadian.\n\nAnnual Reports\nReach Report: 2025/26 Fiscal Year\nView Report\nReach Report: 2024/25 Fiscal Year\nView Report\n\nHistorica Canada is a charitable organization that offers programs in both official languages that you can use to explore, learn, reflect on our history, and consider what it means to be Canadian.\n\nHistorica Canada's business number is 885434720RR0001\n\nAbout Us\nPolicies\nCareers\nHistorica Canada Content Usage Request Form\n\nFollow Us\nMore From Historica Canada\nCitizenship Challenge\nHeritage Minutes\nThe Memory Project\nThe Canadian Encyclopedia\nPartnership: The World Remembers\n© Historica Canada 2026. All rights reserved.\nWebsite by DS"
